s nothing. Nothing else moves: the peak stays below the unchanged 5.0 m main-wall head, and the dormer plan extent, the light, the lower sash, the connector, the turned range, the main block, the footprint and the world placement are untouched. The shoulder roof silhouette and the left group's relative proportions remain OPEN on T-2376.\n\n SHOULDER ROOF RISE TRIAL, 2026-11-09: the existing roof_high_m working control rises from 4.0 to 4.6 m at the main-block attachment, retaining the outer roof_low_m 3.2 m. Across the unchanged 3.6 m shoulder span this steepens the shed from about 12.5 to 21.3 degrees, following the stronger rise toward the main wall visible behind the little pointed light in Andreas. These are RECONSTRUCTED trial controls for relative form, not dimensions measured from the retrospective drawing, and establish no historical alteration or July-1835 stage. The accepted 4.85 m pointed cap, its light and lower sash, the 2.8 m shoulder wall, all three component spans/depths/occupied polygons and their turn, the main building and its surveyed placement remain unchanged. Existing source disagreement with Trowbridge\u2019s open bay remains explicit. The actual new native mesh, unchanged-camera comparison and published compound review are still required; original T-2376 remains open and the broader left-group proportions are not signed off by this one slope trial."
